{"name":"Playful Peach","hex":"#fce3ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"playful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Enjoying play; sportive; prone to playing frequently, in the manner of a child or young pet (viz. puppy or kitten).","Funny; humorous; jesty; frolicsome; frisky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playful"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Play (activity)","blocks":[{"text":"Play is a range of intrinsically motivated activities done for recreation. Play is commonly associated with children and juvenile-level activities, but may be engaged in at any life stage, and among other higher-functioning animals as well, most notably mammals and birds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Playfulness_by_Paul_Manship%2C_1912-1914_-_DSC03107.JPG/330px-Playfulness_by_Paul_Manship%2C_1912-1914_-_DSC03107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Play_(activity)","wikidata":"Q1150958"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach","wikidata":"Q13189"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)","wikidata":"Q5148721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/500px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/1280px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/500px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"People having fun","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJuly_4th_Traditions_(7188250241).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/500px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/1280px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/500px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A three-legged race is a form of competition that requires cooper